---
const reasons = [
  {
    title: "You run a large-production stage",
    body: "If you feed SDI or NDI to cameras, a broadcast mixer, or a big LED wall, ProPresenter's pro video I/O is built for that and we're not there yet.",
  },
  {
    title: "You rely on a cue or scheduling system",
    body: "ProPresenter lets you script a tightly-timed service with cues. We don't have that yet.",
  },
  {
    title: "You live in Planning Center",
    body: "If your service order, songs, and volunteers already flow through Planning Center Online, ProPresenter imports straight from it. We don't integrate with PCO yet.",
  },
  {
    title: "You depend on CCLI SongSelect",
    body: "ProPresenter pulls songs from SongSelect and helps with copyright reporting. We don't do either yet. We do provide importing from other sources.",
  },
];
---

<section>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="py-12 md:py-20 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="text-center pb-10">
          <h2 class="h2 font-red-hat-display mb-4">What's the catch?</h2>
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
            If any of the following describes you, ProPresenter is the better
            option for you, for now.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
          {
            reasons.map((reason, i) => (
              <div
                class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 p-5"
                data-aos="fade-up"
                data-aos-delay={(i % 2) * 100}
              >
                <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100 mb-2">
                  {reason.title}
                </h3>
                <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-sm">
                  {reason.body}
                </p>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>

        <p
          class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-8 text-center"
          data-aos="fade-up"
        >
          If that's you, this isn't the right switch today. For everyone else,
          there's no reason to keep paying. The
          <a
            href="/compare/propresenter-alternative"
            class="text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400 hover:underline font-medium"
            >full comparison</a
          > goes through every feature, in both directions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
